    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\nDetails:\n- See PR [42793](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42793) in neovim/neovim\n\nFailing test: T['Align with preview']['works'], only when parametrized with 'Normal-*'. In the fifth screenshot the command line is not cleared.\n\nI replayed the test manually step by step and everything seems to work correctly. So, perhaps this is 'rpc' related. I could not apply a fix in the test itself unfortunately. An extra `H.unecho()` does the trick. Perhaps there is a better solution?\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-12T16:38:23Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The fix might be simpler:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n\r\nH.unecho = function()\r\n  -- if H.cache.msg_shown then vim.cmd([[echo '' | redraw]]) end\r\n  if H.cache.msg_shown then vim.cmd([[redraw | echo '']]) end\r\nend\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nAll tests in test_align succeed using all supported Neovim versions. I also ran the failing test by hand. After pressing `<CR>`, the command line is cleared as expected.",
            "created_at": "2026-11-12T09:17:21Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2597#issuecomment-6819649775",
